Description: gamdid provides inference and interpretable visualizations for
    comparing distributions in single cell proteomics data. It recasts the
    problem of density estimation as a Poisson regression and leverages the
    GAM framework of the mgcv package to flexibly model distributions and
    generate a GAM p-value. This GAM p-value is aggregated with the msqrob2
    p-value via the harmonic mean p-value to improve power for mean shifts.
    The GAM fits support interpretable visualization and detection of
    differential regions in the distribution. gamdid also supports omnibus
    testing across more than two groups, with post-hoc pairwise comparisons
    via stagewise testing.
